       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 50 mg is five times the usual maximum daily dose of amlodipine, which is 10 mg. Typical dosing is 2.5\u201310 mg once daily. At 50 mg, the risks include severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and prolonged vasodilatory shock. Amlodipine's half-life is long, so those effects could last a long time.\n\nPlease check whether one of these applies:\n- **Typo:** Did you mean 5 mg or 10 mg once daily?\n- **Unit or transcription error:** Was another drug or dose intended?\n- **Deliberate dose:** If 50 mg is intended, tell me the rationale and I'll enter it with a note. I'd still suggest confirming with pharmacy first.\n\nOnce you confirm the dose, I'll enter the order right away. For example, I can enter amlodipine 5 mg PO once daily."
